dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.11013,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":73.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Korsana Biosciences, Inc. develops therapeutic antibodies for the treatment of neurodegenerative diseases. The company has developed Therapeutic Targeting (THETA), a blood-brain barrier-penetrant shuttle platform designed to enhance central nervous system exposure of investigational therapies and enable delivery of large therapeutic molecules across the blood-brain barrier into the central nervous system. The company advances a pipeline of THETA-enabled therapeutics with an initial focus on neurodegenerative disorders. Its lead product candidate is KRSA-028, an anti-amyloid beta antibody for the treatment of Alzheimer's disease, which combines the THETA platform with elements of anti-amyloid beta approaches and targets a clinically relevant form of amyloid beta designed to improve brain uptake while reducing effects on reticulocytes. The company is also advancing a pipeline of additional THETA-enabled therapies for other neurodegenerative diseases. Korsana Biosciences, Inc. was incorporated in 2024 and is based in Waltham, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Jonathan  Violin M.B.A., Ph.D. | President, CEO, Secretary & Director | Age 50","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19 people. Revenue per employee of $109K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, declining at 12%/yr \u2014 weakening productivity. Stock-based compensation of $23K per employee reflects an ownership culture.","financial_summary":["Korsana Biosciences, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.4B market cap on $2M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -19% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -348% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","Net dilution runs at 0.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 21% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 240% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthcare sector